# cella.policy — the crossings this task is granted.
# One grant per line: allow <direction> <ip>:<port>/<proto>
#                  or allow <direction> <ethertype>
# '*' matches any ip or any port. Everything not granted is refused.
#
# Every grant is exact on purpose, and every flow is a round trip at
# this border: the request parks outgoing and the reply parks in the
# ingress lane (docs/EXAMPLES.md E1), so a granted destination needs
# its reply twin -- measured: with only the outgoing grant, the SYN
# released and the SYN-ACK lapsed refused. Same for ARP: the guest's
# request goes out, the translator's answer comes in. Everything else
# the guest attempts is refused, with the why on the machine's record.
allow outgoing arp
allow incoming arp
allow outgoing 1.1.1.1:443/tcp
allow incoming 1.1.1.1:443/tcp
